FineWine: ray queries on Metal acceleration structures

Adds VK_KHR_acceleration_structure and VK_KHR_ray_query to MoltenVK 1.4.2, on macOS 15 and
later with a GPU that supports ray tracing.

- VkAccelerationStructureKHR is a Metal acceleration structure. Bottom-level structures take
  triangle and bounding-box geometry straight from the application's buffers; top-level
  structures have their instances converted to Metal's layout on the CPU, so the instance
  data must be in host-visible memory.
- Builds, updates (as Metal refits), copies (clone and compact), build sizes and device
  addresses are implemented. Host builds and serialisation are not.
- An acceleration structure descriptor is stored in the argument buffer like a texture, by
  resource id. Only Metal 3 argument buffers are supported.
- Ray tracing pipelines (VK_KHR_ray_tracing_pipeline) are not part of this.

The new .mm files are included from MVKBuffer.mm and MVKCmdDispatch.mm so that the Xcode
project does not change.

